    {
      "id": "claim_add6d15fdb174f63a83d1ea5a2051bee",
      "statement": "RaindropService and RaindropApiClientImpl are split into separate beans specifically so that business-rule validation (configuration/enabled checks, collection selection) runs outside the Resilience4j circuit breaker/retry, while only RaindropApiClientImpl's HTTP calls carry @CircuitBreaker(name=\"raindrop\") and @Retry(name=\"raindrop\") annotations; this avoids Spring AOP self-invocation bypassing the proxy if the annotated methods lived on RaindropService itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropApiClientImpl.java#L13-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3eabbfd7c61a1dc13a6b64b87cb5e3ebdd4fe0447326623086fe8037271d2337:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropService.java#L18-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7efe1683706930a37e847950312b27d17aab8b75f8f0a6ed3645ff39908f048c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e0833c7db9f6429284293f005202ab91",
      "statement": "RaindropApiClientImpl's listCollectionsFallback and createBookmarkFallback methods explicitly check `throwable instanceof RaindropNotConfiguredException` and rethrow it unchanged, while wrapping every other throwable as IllegalStateException(\"Raindrop.io is currently unavailable\", throwable), so that RaindropNotConfiguredException reaches GlobalExceptionHandler distinctly instead of being swallowed into a generic circuit-breaker failure.",
