    {
      "id": "claim_2339b18787cc4a3e99e5e287714209f7",
      "statement": "The Jev (TypeSafe) integration follows the same aspect-ordering convention as Raindrop (business/configuration checks before the annotated call, resilience annotations on a dedicated client bean) but its judge() method is annotated with @CircuitBreaker(name=\"jev\")/@Retry(name=\"jev\") and deliberately has no fallbackMethod at all, so typed TypeSafe exceptions and CallNotPermittedException propagate unchanged rather than being selectively rethrown via a fallback like Raindrop's.",
